<!--
beet_@name@'s entry: `just cli` discovers it, builds it, and the root's
`CallOnReady` calls it with the process request, dispatching down into the
router. A route naming a type defined in this crate resolves because the binary
links `@Name@Plugin`; the stock `beet` cannot, hence the `<RequireCfg>`.

    just cli --help
-->
<CliServer {CallOnReady}>
<Router {(RequestLogger, HelpHandler)}>
	<RequireCfg cfg="feature:cli"/>
</Router>
</CliServer>
